Change: The interface language follows the browser unless a user chose one

Without `default_language`, ownCloud stored the language of the first visit
permanently for every user. A later visit with a browser in another language
kept the old language, and a client without an Accept-Language header could
fix an account to English.

The browser language now applies on every visit. It is still remembered per
user for e-mails and background jobs, but marked as taken from the browser, so
the next visit with another browser language replaces it. A language chosen
under personal settings always wins, and so do all language settings that
existed before this change. German browser variants (de, de-AT, de-CH) get
formal German (de_DE), so the form of address no longer depends on the
browser. English remains the last resort.
